  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is the strongest RNA encoder (config_005: 0.650 acc vs config_002: 0.591 for pca_n2000), avgpool beats transformer for aggregation, and multiprofile beats singleprofile. Surprisingly, adding resnet50 image with concat fusion to the scvi_n200 multimodal model (config_030: 0.632) slightly underperforms the RNA-only version (config_005: 0.650), whereas with pca_n2000 the multimodal concat helped (config_018: 0.619 > config_002: 0.591). This suggests the concat fusion may be the bottleneck when the RNA signal is already strong. Question: Does weighted fusion resolve the multimodal underperformance with scvi_n200? config_031 changes only the fusion strategy (concat→weighted) relative to config_030, giving a clean A/B test of fusion. Why this is best: it isolates a single design variable, directly addresses the most surprising finding (multimodal < unimodal with the best encoder), and determines whether the image modality is salvageable with better fusion or fundamentally unhelpful—critical information before investing further experiments in multimodal variants."
}

